nths ago so yeah  just a brief comment there I guess that  that language learning shouldn't be an  obligation language learning is a very  it can be with the right approach a very  enjoyable activity very beneficial  activity is the brain and my preference  is to not content yourself with the sort  of hello how are you and why look at me  i could say things in 10 languages but  all i can say is hello and at the other  end no don't impose yourself on yourself  some obligation would be perfect make  mistakes as long as you can communicate  that's the goal and in that sense to  just well I'm suddenly had another  thought getting back to the whole  testing thing yeah I recognize that  there is a need for some standard  testing but I must say that I think  testing in language is not a useful  thing the only thing that you should  measure if I were student the only thing  I would measure is is the student  spending the time with the language some  people learn faster similar slower more  slowly some things will fall in place  earlier some things will fall in place  later the only thing you should really  be worried about is this person  listening is this person reading is his  person enjoying himself or herself is  are they spending the time on the task  and that's the only thing that really  matters anyway I might just do this in  in French or in some other language as  well
 

